<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  DEBUG-BUILD-ONLY override of src/main/res/xml/network_security_config.xml,
  via Android's standard src/debug/ source-set overlay (Gradle merges this
  IN PLACE of the main one for any `debug` build variant — never present in
  a release build at all, so this file can't accidentally widen what a real
  signed release APK is allowed to do).

  Earlier attempt used <debug-overrides><base-config .../></debug-overrides>
  inside the main config — confirmed WRONG against Android's own docs
  (developer.android.com/privacy-and-security/security-config):
  <debug-overrides> may only contain a single optional <trust-anchors>
  element, nothing else. It silently doesn't do what you'd expect otherwise
  (reproduced: Mixed Content still blocked the request even with debuggable
  builds and that structure in place). A plain source-set overlay, unlike
  that, is unambiguous and easy to verify (this file exists only for debug
  builds, period).

  See src/main/res/xml/network_security_config.xml for why this is needed
  at all (Capacitor's https://localhost origin + Mixed Content blocking a
  local plain-http dev/QA server) and why it's safe for the real production
  APK (which is HTTPS already, regardless of what's cleartext-permitted).
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
